ch.)\n\n## Verification (my own commands, not self-reports)\n- `cargo build --release` — clean, no warnings.\n- **Completion gate:** `nm -D --defined-only` on both `.so` files, diffed on name *and* binding type, both directions → **empty diff**.\n- **Differential harness:** `dlopen`s each `.so` and compares 90 `extractFilename` cases (15 paths × 6 separators, including `'\\0'`) and 600 `FIO_createFilename_fromOutDir` cases (15 paths × 10 out-dirs × 4 suffix lens), dumping the **entire allocation byte-for-byte** to also prove zero-fill parity → **692/692 lines byte-identical**. All 600 pointers were `free()`d with no crash, confirming allocator compatibility.\n- **Edge cases:** the OOB `outDirName[-1]` read tested with a heap buffer where I control the preceding byte (`/`, `X`, `.`) — both libs pick the same branch; and the `calloc`-failure path (`suffixLen = SIZE_MAX-16`) — both print `zstd: FIO_createFilename_fromOutDir: Cannot allocate memory` and exit `30`.\n\nOne note on process: my first harness run showed 10 differing lines. Those turned out to be my harness's own bug — it sized the hex dump with `strlen(path)` instead of `strlen(filenameStart)`, so it read past the buffer into glibc heap metadata (`0x51`, `0xd1`, chunk-size bytes). I fixed the harness rather than the translation; the re-run was clean. `c_src/` is untouched."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":722,"cache_read_input_tokens":32801,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":722,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":9,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"983591dc-28cf-48fa-9d50-99bc489dd9b7","uuid":"083ba0c0-ae76-463e-a270-da27ed850e68","timestamp":"2026-08-20T04:32:34.066Z"}
